{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_367","type":"reasoning","text":"The lifecycle check pre-existing failures are 4 files unrelated to mine (harness-gap-envelope-reject, harness-gap-paired-ablation, harness-gap-reliability-aggregation, harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling). My new spec has lifecycleStatus: archived, so it passes.\n\nNow let me reconsider acceptance criterion 5: \"干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。\" I can't run vitest/typecheck/lint because there's no node_modules and I'm told not to install. I've documented this honestly. That's the correct handling.\n\nWait — but I created a new rule spec `harness/specs/rules/sensitive-sink-ledger-boundary.md` and referenced it in the task spec's `requiredRules`. The validate passed, and context resolved it (it appeared in the read order). Good.\n\nLet me double check one concern: the task spec's `requiredTests` lists `tests/unit/sensitive-sink-residual-ledger.test.ts`. Does harness validate require the test file to exist? Let me check — validate passed, so no issue.\n\nAlso, let me reconsider whether my reverse-sweep in the test could be too strict. It requires every runtime source file importing `isExternalOrUnknownProvenance` to be registered in the ledger. Currently exactly 6 importers, all registered. But wait — registration uses `policyFile` and `callSite`. The 6 importers are all policyFiles. Good.\n\nOne risk: the reverse sweep scans `openclaw_runtime/src` recursively reading every `.ts` file (~4792 files, 583ms). That's fine for a unit test.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the hidden oracle. The task says \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" The hidden oracle might add `tests/unit/sensitive-sink-enforcement-drift.test.ts` (referenced in comments). My test doesn't conflict.\n\nNow, let me reconsider acceptance criterion 2's exact list: \"outbound-send-service / message-action-dispatch / cli-runtime outbound / sessions send-policy / auto-reply send-policy / server-broadcast\". My surfaces match exactly: outbound-send-service, message-action-dispatch, cli-runtime-outbound, sessions-send-policy, auto-reply-send-policy, server-broadcast. Good.\n\nLet me verify the ledger doc contains each residual surface name and file. The probe already checked that. \n\nLet me also double-check the `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/README` doc index requirement — docs-index.test.ts checks top-level docs markdown files in `docs/`, not `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/`. So no index update needed.\n\nAlso check-dup-assets requires git — can't run (no .git). Documented.\n\nLet me verify the acceptance JSON's `residualNetworkSendEgress` order matches the test's expectation. Test expects the surfaces array equal to RESIDUAL_NETWORK_SEND_EGRESS.map(surface). The probe verified. Good.\n\nLet me now re-verify the SHA256SUMS contents and that the doc genuinely contains the token and all six surfaces/files (probe already did). Also confirm the ledger mentions \"不是全网强制\".\n\nLet me do a final read of the ledger doc to confirm quality."}}
