{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_372","type":"reasoning","text":"Each residual surface appears once in the ledger (in the residual table). Good. The test asserts ledger contains the surface and file. Good.\n\nEverything is verified. Let me do a final sanity check that the acceptance JSON has `wholeNetworkEnforcement: false` and the residual list order matches.\n\nAlready verified via probe ALL PASS. \n\nLet me now write the final structured result. The result schema requires status, summary, testsRun.\n\nLet me double check I haven't left any stray files in the workspace. Let me list any untracked-looking files I created.\n\nFiles created:\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s02-sink-ledger.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s02-acceptance.json\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S02-SHA256SUMS\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-sink-ledger.md\n- harness/specs/rules/sensitive-sink-ledger-boundary.md\n- tests/unit/sensitive-sink-residual-ledger.test.ts\n\nStray probe deleted. Good.\n\nLet me verify the test file content once more for the credential regex — the file contains the literal regex `sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}` etc. Does the credential scan regex match its own pattern text? The pattern `sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}` requires 16+ alphanumerics after `sk-`. In the test file the text is `sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}` — after `sk-` comes `[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}` which is not 16 alphanumerics (it has brackets/braces). So no self-match. Good. And the earlier credential scan reported 0 hits, confirming.\n\nAlso check: the source-inventory / other evidence referencing. The docs-sync rule: no README change needed. \n\nOne more consideration: harness validate runs the changed-path ownership gate for scenario-bound tasks. When run with `--no-diff` it passed. Without --no-diff in this workspace there is no git, so it will error on diff base. The acceptance notes acknowledge this. Good.\n\nI should double-check that my test's `readdirSync` of `openclaw_runtime/src` won't be too slow. The timing measured 583ms for full walk reading all files. That's fine within vitest 30s timeout.\n\nActually wait — my test's `listRuntimeSourceFiles` reads every file (4792 files) once for the reverse sweep, plus `readRepoFile` again. The probe did the same and it took <1s. Good.\n\nLet me finalize.\n\nLet me confirm the exact list of testsRun to report. I'll report the checks I actually ran, distinguishing pass / not-run.\n\nActually, I need to also double check the acceptance JSON's `residualNetworkSendEgress` order matches RESIDUAL array order in test: outbound-send-service, message-action-dispatch, cli-runtime-outbound, sessions-send-policy, auto-reply-send-policy, server-broadcast. In the JSON I wrote: outbound-send-service, message-action-dispatch, cli-runtime-outbound, sessions-send-policy, auto-reply-send-policy, server-broadcast. Yes matches. Probe confirmed ALL PASS.\n\nDone. Write final answer."}}
