{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_377","type":"agent_message","text":"All deliverables are in place and verified. Here's the structured result.\n\n**Status: completed**\n\n**Summary**\n\nS02 (`tf-0277-s02`, slot HG16) implements an executable sensitive-sink coverage ledger with a residual network-send egress guard. I did **not** build a second provenance engine: the ledger is an accounting/verification layer over the existing `shared/security/content-provenance.ts`, which is left unchanged.\n\nDelivered artifacts:\n- `tests/unit/sensitive-sink-residual-ledger.test.ts` — the executable half. Resolves every declared enforcement point (policyFile, exported symbol, production call site, denial style) against the working tree; pins the `network-send` gate to exactly the cross-context outbound policy; pins six residual egress surfaces as *outside* the gate; reverse-sweeps the runtime so any new provenance import must be registered; re-reads `S02-SHA256SUMS`; and scans for credential shapes.\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s02-sink-ledger.md` — per-sink ledger (narrow / source-dependent) with authoritative code refs, the six residual exits, and an explicit `NOT-WHOLE-NETWORK-ENFORCEMENT` statement (\"不是全网强制\").\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s02-acceptance.json` — `wholeNetworkEnforcement: false`, seven sink rows, six residual surfaces with `provenanceReferences: 0`, and honest gate status.\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-sink-ledger.md` + `harness/specs/rules/sensitive-sink-ledger-boundary.md` — spec and rule.\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S02-SHA256SUMS` — verifies clean.\n\nVerified facts from code (not self-report): sinks `secret-read`, `network-send`, `external-write`, `browser-effect`(×2), `credential-use` reject (policy-throw / call-site-throw); `command-exec` only constrains; the sole `network-send` gate is `enforceCrossContextPolicy` in `outbound-policy.ts` called from `message-action-runner.ts`. The six residuals (`outbound-send-service`, `message-action-dispatch`, cli-runtime `channel-outbound-send`, `sessions/send-policy`, `auto-reply/send-policy`, `server-broadcast`) each contain **zero** provenance references.\n\n**Tests run** (exact commands and outcomes):\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-sink-ledger.md --no-diff` → exit 0, \"Spec is valid\"\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs context --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-sink-ledger.md` → exit 0, no missing scenarios/rules\n- `sha256sum -c docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S02-SHA256SUMS` → exit 0, all 5 files OK\n- `node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs` → exit 0, `ok`\n- `node scripts/check-evidence-refs.mjs` → exit 0, `PASS 157 referenced path(s)`\n- Equivalent offline probe (`node --experimental-strip-types`, dependency-free replay of the vitest assertions: kind set, per-sink point resolution, reverse sweep, residual pinning, manifest re-read) → `ALL PASS`\n- Credential scan over the six artifacts (sk-/AKIA/ghp_/xox/bearer/private-key patterns) → 0 hits\n\nNot run (recorded honestly, not claimed as passed):\n- `vitest run tests/unit/sensitive-sink-residual-ledger.test.ts`, `pnpm run typecheck`, `eslint` — this isolated workspace has no `node_modules`, and dependencies were not to be installed. The test file itself parses cleanly under Node (only `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: vitest`).\n- `harness run --dry-run` — the workspace has no `.git`, so the default diff base `origin/main` doesn't resolve.\n- Pre-existing: `pnpm harness:specs:lifecycle` reports 4 unrelated specs missing `lifecycleStatus` (`harness-gap-envelope-reject`, `-paired-ablation`, `-reliability-aggregation`, `-trace-cost-sampling`); not introduced by S02.\n\nNo product defaults/locks/approvals changed; README four-locale review found no user-visible interface change, so READMEs are unchanged. Evidence is labeled `driven_by: agent`."}}
